  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Impact Cluster: VEG Impact Myanmar</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The VEG Impact Myanmar project will contribute towards the growth and development of the vegetable sector in Myanmar and will deliver impact in terms of:&#x2022;	Enhanced local capacities for realising the growth potential of the Myanmar vegetable sector;&#x2022;	Sustainable productivity and income improvements for male and female smallholder vegetable producers;&#x2022;	Increased supplies of safe vegetables to the markets in and around Myanmar.This project exists of the following organisations and companies:&#x2022;	The Ministry of Agriculture, Livestock &amp; Irrigation and its regional research farms as main public sector partner;&#x2022;	The Vegetable Sector Acceleration Taskforce (VSAT) as project&#x2019;s Steering Committee;&#x2022;	RVO programme VEG CAP (Knowledge-to-knowledge (K2K));&#x2022;	State Agricultural Institutes (SAIs); and&#x2022;	Yezin Agricultural University and local partners (e.g. the Myanmar Onion, Garlic and Culinary Crops Production &amp; Exporting Association; Dagon International and the Myanmar Agro Exchange Public Co., LTD. (MAEX) as owner and manager of the modern Yangon wholesale market for fresh produce).</narrative>
  </description>
